// An arithmetic policy on an array's ELEMENT type keeps the whole-array
// store row: `i32 in Wrapping` qualifies arithmetic on the stored value,
// never its storage shape, so the policy-constrained element is still a
// closed primitive carrier. The same policy on the ARRAY was always peeled
// for the same reason; the element peel now matches it. Reduced from
// `samples/cli/collections/matrix_multiply`.
//
//   [i32; 3]               <- [1, 2, 3]   checks
//   [u8; 3]                <- [1, 2, 3]   checks
//   [i32; 3] in Wrapping   <- [1, 2, 3]   checks    <- policy on the ARRAY
//   [i32 in Wrapping; 3]   <- [1, 2, 3]   checks    <- policy on the ELEMENT
//   [i32 in Saturating; 3] <- [1, 2, 3]   checks
//
// An array whose element is a RECORD or a CASE is not a primitive carrier:
// `main.grid = [Cell { v: 1 }, Cell { v: 2 }]` into `[Cell; 2]` establishes
// each element and replaces its own element window instead
// (`record_array_literal_field_store_exit`,
// `case_array_literal_field_store_exit`; the `grid: [Cell; 24]` of
// `samples/cli/rendering/dungeon_render` is the case customer). A
// predicate-domain element (`[i32 in Ten; 3]`) stays declined: the domain's
// membership evidence is a separate contract, not a storage fact.
//
// Storing ONE element (`main.grid[0][0] = 1`) checks. Storing one ROW
// (`main.grid[0] = [1, 2, 3]`) is now admitted the same way: the literal's
// leaf roster composes through the destination's fixed or runtime index
// segment instead of requiring a whole-field destination.
//
// Local record-field observations have their own native regression at
// `tests/omega/pass/structs/runtime_local_record_policy_exit`.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    row: [i32 in Wrapping; 3];
}

machine Main::main(main: &mut Main) reaches Console {
    main.row = [1, 2, 3];
    main.console.exit_process(0);
}
